Display HAL: answer the flipped (turned by 90 degrees) mode query

The screen driver (CScreenDeviceHelper::DeviceOrientationsAvailable) asks HAL EDisplayOffsetBetweenLines for
the current mode with TSurfaceId's EHalFlippedFlag (0x80000000); our driver refused the negative mode with
KErrArgument, so the screen device offered only 0 and 180 degrees and WSERV refused direct screen access in
a landscape scene ("** Current Rotation Mode not supported by the DSA device"; Assassin's Creed's intro
video retried for ever). Answer with width and height swapped and the stride of a turned line.
Copy the file into the syborgfx and syborgmv variants as well.

--- a/baseport/syborg/fb/syborg_fb.cpp
+++ b/baseport/syborg/fb/syborg_fb.cpp
@@ -238,6 +238,13 @@
 
 TInt DLcdPowerHandler::GetSpecifiedDisplayModeInfo(TInt aMode, TVideoInfoV01& aInfo)
 {
+  // syborg-pg: the flipped flag (TSurfaceId::TScreenSurfaceUsage::EHalFlippedFlag) asks for the mode
+  // turned by 90 degrees. The screen driver reports 90/270 orientations only if this answers
+  // (CScreenDeviceHelper::DeviceOrientationsAvailable), and WSERV refuses direct screen access in a turned
+  // scene otherwise ("Current Rotation Mode not supported by the DSA device": games' intro videos)
+  const TInt KFlipped = (TInt)0x80000000;
+  TBool flipped = (aMode & KFlipped) != 0;
+  aMode &= ~KFlipped;
   if(aMode < 0 || aMode >= KConfigLcdNumberOfDisplayModes)
 	return KErrArgument;
   
@@ -256,6 +263,16 @@
 
 	  aInfo.iBitsPerPixel       = KConfigBitsPerPixel;
 	}
+  if(flipped)
+	{
+	  TInt w = aInfo.iSizeInPixels.iWidth;
+	  aInfo.iSizeInPixels.iWidth = aInfo.iSizeInPixels.iHeight;
+	  aInfo.iSizeInPixels.iHeight = w;
+	  w = aInfo.iSizeInTwips.iWidth;
+	  aInfo.iSizeInTwips.iWidth = aInfo.iSizeInTwips.iHeight;
+	  aInfo.iSizeInTwips.iHeight = w;
+	  aInfo.iOffsetBetweenLines = aInfo.iSizeInPixels.iWidth * 4;	// 32 bpp frame buffer, a turned line
+	}
   return KErrNone;
 }
 
